    <x-sections.prose body="<h2>Work</h2><p>Most of my week goes to a rewrite of Foldwork's build pipeline. It is the least glamorous thing I have worked on in years and easily the most satisfying: every week the feedback loop gets shorter for forty people at once, and you can watch it happen in the graph.</p><h2>Outside work</h2><p>Ledger got a proper query language in June and I have been living on it since, which is the only way I have ever found a design flaw before other people do. Quiet Hours is stable and I am refusing to add history to it, politely, once a week.</p><h2>Reading</h2><p>Slowly through <em>The Timeless Way of Building</em> for the second time, and finding it much better and much stranger than I remembered. Also a lot of railway history, for no reason I can defend.</p><h2>Not doing</h2><p>Conferences, for now. Contract work. Anything that requires me to have an opinion about the future of the industry.</p>" />
